      "note": "Celiac Trunk (T12): Supplies foregut via Left Gastric, Common Hepatic, and Splenic arteries. Superior Mesenteric Artery (L1): Supplies midgut (distal duodenum to proximal 2/3 transverse colon) via Inferior Pancreaticoduodenal, Intestinal branches, Ileocolic, Right Colic, and Middle Colic arteries. Inferior Mesenteric Artery (L3): Supplies hindgut (distal 1/3 transverse colon to upper rectum) via Left Colic, Sigmoid, and Superior Rectal arteries. Renal Arteries (L1-L2): Bilateral direct branches from abdominal aorta supplying kidneys and adrenals."
